comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-14T05:42:15.462Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 1 (Greptile P1, Codex P2/P3), fixed: (1) The merge driver merges deferred_fields by field, not by whole-element identity. A one-sided addition survives, a deletion (resolution) wins, and a reason both sides changed differently resolves by stable value order in either merge direction. Two branches with different reasons for one field previously produced a document the parser refuses (duplicate field). (2) Explicit --deadline/--assignee/--ac/--estimate values or unsets on create --stdin-json now override the document's deferral of that field instead of failing with create_deferral_conflict. (3) The error catalog attributes the create_deferral_* codes to the create command (generator module map). Specs extended in tests/unit/sdk/lifecycle/create-deferrals.spec.ts."
  "2026-11-14T06:10:56.045Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 2 (Codex), fixed: (1) On a strict tracker, rolling back a deferred create was refused twice over. The compensation close went through strict close validation, and a create that used the --clear-* options hid the transaction's apply marker behind its ' | explicit_unset=...' suffix (filed and fixed as pm-chdp87). Compensation closes now pass validateClose off, since a rollback close completes no work. (2) After the field-keyed union, the merge driver prunes any deferral whose field holds a concrete merged value, in the item merge and the history-union projection alike. (3) A runtime schema field whose metadata key is a deferrable field (due mapped to deadline) now conflicts with a deferral of that field, both in create and in the stdin-json override. (4) The close refusal's pm update recovery carries --author=<the close's author>, so strict ownership accepts the corrective update. Negative control: without the compensation fix, the strict rollback spec fails."
  "2026-11-14T06:34:03.946Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 3 (Codex, Greptile, CodeRabbit). Four findings fixed: (1) commitImportedItem prunes deferrals that the imported document resolves before stamping, guards and persistence, matching the item-store write path. (2) On stdin-json create, an --unset of a schema field mapped to a deferrable key (due, its cli flag, or an alias) drops the document deferral of that key. (3) A deferral drops template defaults of schema fields mapped to that key. A caller's explicit value is kept, so the conflict check still fires. (4) The close refusal's recovery carries --force alongside --author. Kept by design: an explicit --defer-reason supplied together with a document's reasonless deferral applies to it, because the caller's own reason is explicit and auditable. The round-2 fix was about one document entry silently borrowing another entry's reason."
  "2026-11-14T06:50:10.362Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 4 (Codex), fixed: (1) A schema field with required_on_create whose metadata key is a deferrable field (due mapped to deadline) is now satisfied by a deferral of that key, as the type-level requirement is (withoutDeferredRuntimeRequirements). (2) On stdin-json create, an explicit reason in any spelling (deferReason or the defer_reason alias) is never replaced by a reason synthesized from the document."
  "2026-11-14T07:00:49.515Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 5 (Codex P1), fixed: the round-4 relaxation also suppressed schema fields with required: true. Those require the value on every stored record, so the item would persist and then fail item_document_invalid on the next read. Only create-only required_on_create requirements now yield to a deferral; a stored-record requirement keeps refusing the create. Covered by spec."
  "2026-11-14T07:15:35.376Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 6 (Codex, Greptile, CodeRabbit), fixed: (1) The deferral exemption covers only create-scoped schema definitions, and it keeps any flag another create requirement still needs, so a shared flag spelling can never hide an unrelated stored-required field. (2) On stdin-json create, unset tokens resolve through the shared create unset resolver (resolveRuntimeUnsetFieldDefinition), accepting the same uppercase and underscore spellings. (3) Template defaults are dropped under every candidate option key of a schema field mapped to the deferred key (resolveCandidateOptionKeys: key, flag and aliases in each spelling). Kept by design: creating an item directly in a terminal status may carry deferrals. That path mirrors work finished in another system, it already bypasses close-evidence validation, and refusing it would re-break the strict importer sync for every closed upstream issue. The deferral stays listed as curation work in validate and health."
  "2026-11-14T07:50:23.534Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 7 (Codex), fixed: (1) The stdin-json adapter resolves unsets with create's own parser (parseCreateUnsetTargets now lives in shared-unset-fields.ts and is shared by create and the adapter). Resolution is core alias first, then schema fields, with whole-token expansion, so a schema key spelled ac can no longer drop the deadline deferral. (2) Schema-field overrides of document deferrals and of template defaults consider only create-scoped fields. (3) The shared-flag guard keeps a flag only for another genuinely required create definition, not an optional one. Also: the actor clone moved to the dependency-free mutation-actor-snapshot.ts, and the resolver loads lazily when a guard runs. The local entrypoint-cost bench is noisy on this host (main fails it too: ./sdk/authoring 172 ms against 164 ms); CI passed it on earlier heads."
  "2026-11-14T08:07:09.277Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 8 (Codex), fixed: the first-party pm-todos export/import round trip rebuilt metadata without deferred_fields, which silently dropped the audit trail and the strict-close protection. A new SDK import helper, toImportDeferredFields, keeps one valid, reasoned entry per deferrable field. The todos mapping passes it through, and commitImportedItem stamps format 4. ItemDeferredField is exported from ./sdk and ./sdk/runtime."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-14T04:32:04.757Z","harness:claude-code","Design (2026-11-14): deferral is typed item metadata deferred_fields [{field, reason}] (src/core/item/deferred-fields.ts declares the deferrable set as data: deadline, assignee, acceptance_criteria, estimated_minutes; repeatables already have --clear-*). Stored deferrals require item format 4, so a host that predates them refuses the record instead of dropping the entries and letting strict close pass. Create: --defer (repeatable, comma lists) + required --defer-reason (SDK defer[]/deferReason, MCP pm_create), parsed in src/sdk/lifecycle/create-deferrals.ts; a deferred option satisfies the strict required check; deferring a field also set or unset is create_deferral_conflict; a deferral drops the template default like an unset. Resolution: mutateItem prunes any entry whose field gained a value on the same write (covers update, update-many, claim, stdin-json). Close: outstanding deferrals refuse --validate-close strict with close_validation_deferred_fields (recovery is a runnable pm update) and warn otherwise. Curation: validate --check-metadata adds details.deferred_fields + validate_metadata_deferred_fields:<n>; health reports integrity details.curation informationally only, so strict fleet trackers running pm health --check-only in CI do not turn red. Creating directly in a terminal status with a deferral is allowed (it mirrors work finished elsewhere) and stays listed as curation work."
  "2026-11-14T05:21:44.115Z","harness:claude-code","Side effect handled in scope (2026-11-14): adding deferred_fields to the item key order pushed the pm list --fields refusal from 1,9xx to 2,025 estimated tokens, over the 2,000-token recovery-bundle budget. The ladder then dropped why and examples and cut allowed_values to 3 entries. The cause was that list doubled its legal domain with an item.-prefixed copy of every field. The list refusal and its closed-domain contract now name each field once (listCanonicalListProjectionFields) and state the item. alias in required. The refusal fits undegraded again, with all 78 fields and its examples. listListProjectionFields still returns every accepted spelling. get and search keep their domains; for search, item.<field> differs from search-row fields. Also in scope: deferred_fields joins ITEM_UNION_COLLECTION_FIELDS so concurrent resolutions union-merge, and the stdin-json document adapter treats it as read-only on update and maps it to defer/deferReason on create (pm-o74zyh)."
